<title>JAPAN: Sega to start selling digital cameras.</title>
<headline>Sega to start selling digital cameras.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sega Enterprises Ltd said on Wednesday that it plans to start selling digital cameras in Japan in November.  </p>
<p>The camera, called the Digio, will be priced at 29,800 yen, which would make it the cheapest digital camera sold in Japan, a Sega spokesman said.</p>
<p>The company plans to sell 150,000 of the cameras in the current fiscal year ending on March 31, 1997.</p>
</text>
